@huangtingwei9988 @xiezhq-hermann thanks for the merge from main and the run-ci. The base-a red in test_mem_pool_host.py is from this PR. test_double_alloc puts a used slot at the head of free_slots, and the contiguous run lookup in alloc() picks the free run behind it, so the double-alloc assert never fired (the retry then got None because the pool was used up by then).

I pushed f3448061 on top of your merge. alloc() now also checks the head slots that first-fit would have handed out, so a leaked slot there trips the assert again, and I added a small test for the contiguous pick. Locally test_mem_pool_host.py was 21/22 before and is 23/23 now, and the whole unit/mem_cache dir fails the same set as main in my env. CI on that commit stopped at the min-base gate (60878c3f went into main after your merge), so I merged main once more in ca5086fa, no conflicts and main didnt touch the PR files.

The other reds look unrelated to me. AMD tracing, kda and minimax_indexer_cp fail the same way on other PRs today, the mi35x kda/mxfp8 jobs are kernel tests that never build the host pool, a few mi300 jobs died with "runner lost communication", and the NPU HiCache failure is in pool_host/mha.py which this PR doesnt touch (all NPU base-b jobs are red on other PRs too).

